ives/edgar/data/77476/000007747623000023/pep-20230325.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "PEP_10Q_2023-03-25__mdna__0031", "ticker": "PEP", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2023", "period_end": "2023-03-25", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.0069, "filing_name": "PepsiCo Inc 10-Q Q1 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000007747623000023/pep-20230325.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "PEP_10Q_2023-03-25__unknown__0012", "ticker": "PEP", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2023", "period_end": "2023-03-25", "section": "unknown", "score": 0.0067, "filing_name": "PepsiCo Inc 10-Q Q1 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000007747623000023/pep-20230325.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 35, "dropped_candidates": 178, "token_estimate": 31951, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Both companies describe overlapping risk themes: economic conditions, input-cost and supply volatility, health and reputation concerns, product safety, and regulation. Coca-Cola's fiscal 2024 10-K (ended December 31, 2024) highlights reliance on independent bottling partners, which PepsiCo's chunks do not feature [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0020]. PepsiCo's fiscal 2025 10-K (ended December 27, 2025) adds cyber incidents, emerging-market operations, litigation, and credit-rating and exchange-rate risks [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0016][PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0024]. PepsiCo names The Coca-Cola Company as its primary beverage competitor in many countries [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0005]. The filings do not rank risks, and the two periods are a year apart, so comparisons are thematic only; PepsiCo's coverage is a single 10-K.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "KO", "company": "The Coca-Cola Company", "findings": [{"point": "In fiscal 2024 (ended December 31, 2024), the 10-K says a significant portion of revenues comes from selling concentrates and syrups 